    "assignee": null,
    "assignee_team": null,
    "body": "@kasper93 wrote in https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/21226#issuecomment-19534:\r\n\r\n> @Courmisch wrote in #21226 (comment):\r\n> \r\n> > There should be a use before we had some helpers.\r\n> \r\n> Whole `AVInteger` is used in exactly single place in the code base (except tests) in `avidec.c`\r\n> [libavformat/avidec.c](https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/src/commit/d828183d2dd9eb6db236c28c54a198b358668a55/libavformat/avidec.c#L487)\r\n> Line 487 in [d828183](https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/src/commit/d828183d2dd9eb6db236c28c54a198b358668a55)\r\n> ` AVInteger bitrate_i, den_i, num_i; `\r\n> \r\n> which is hardly a necessity there to be used. Also while those functions are part of the ABI, the `integer.h` is not added to `HEADERS` and therefore not installed to be used as part of an avutil public API.\r\n\r\nThis just underlines the point: we should not add internal helpers that are not used at all. This PR should be part of a use case PR, or at least a necessary enabler of another PR before it is submitted.",
